        "## 16. Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "| Phase | Data | What happens |\n",
        "|-------|------|--------------|\n",
        "| **Calibration** | val split | Both models' predictions available → build oracle `escalate` label → tune a confidence-only threshold |\n",
        "| **Inference** | test split | Only small-model uncertainty signals are used → baseline decides keep/escalate |\n",
        "| **Evaluation** | test split | Large-model test preds used **only** to measure routed accuracy (not seen by baseline) |\n",
        "\n",
        "| What | Detail |\n",
        "|------|--------|\n",
        "| **Baseline input** | `small_confidence`, `small_entropy`, `small_margin` |\n",
        "| **Decision rule** | Choose the single best uncertainty signal + threshold on val, then apply that fixed threshold on test |\n",
        "| **Oracle label** | `escalate=1` when small is wrong AND large is correct |\n",
        "| **Model complexity** | No learned router classifier; only threshold calibration |\n",
        "| **Metrics** | Accuracy, Weighted F1, Large-Model Usage %, Avg Cost, Cost Reduction vs Large-Only |\n",
        "| **Cost model** | small = 1 unit, large = 25 units (≈ TinyBERT 14M vs RoBERTa-large 355M params) |\n",
        "| **Cost–accuracy curve** | Threshold sweep for the selected confidence signal showing the trade-off between cost and performance |"
      ]
    }
